			<div class="content" id="post-content-4473714">
									

<p>I absolutely love this. classic deep sea lovecraftian body horror. I suspect some people may accuse this of not being 100% original but there's nothing wrong with embracing and improving upon things :-)</p>
<p>you had me at &quot;Universally, SCP-5000 are composed of groups of between 2 and 9 human bodies fused together amidst large clusters of black tentacles.&quot; O.o good gravy. you reeled me in early into the piece and it was engaging throughout &#8212; i didn't want to stop, i didn't want it to end! my only complaint in terms of writing quality is that I think the very ending could have been a little punchier. to be honest, it felt out of place after that epic article. it just seemed&#8230; anticlimactic. i don't think it ought to be removed but i think it could be improved upon.</p>
<p>I do have a few teensy nitpicks, but its just grammar stuff. normally I'd just go ahead and edit it but idk if you'd want me to do that.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
