<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>&quot;However, on the 19/4/2003&quot;</p>
<p>I notice you've done this with every date but it doesn't make sense w the way the dates are formatted. &quot;on the 19th of april 2003 / on april 19th 2003&quot; makes sense, but &quot;the [numerical date]&quot; feels clunky imo.</p>
<p>&quot;Due to extraneous and irrelevant footages removal and the data corruption present in its later stages of the log, this is not the full record of Exploration 5000-B-38.&quot;</p>
<p>this whole sentence is a bit of a mess. &quot;due to the removal of extraneous footage and significant data corruption in the later stages of the log&quot;&#8230; or something like that, would flow better. (I can probably think of a better way to structure this given time, but I need to hit the hay ASAP)</p>
<p>the beginning of the log in addendum 5000-06 seems to have some wonky formatting w italics &#8212; at the very beginning, things are in italics that i don't think should be based on how the formatting is for the other 3/4 of the log.</p>
